Finding: {"title":"Hour logging silently misattributes to course index 0 when no active course exists","severity":"HIGH","area":"Training plan allocation — hour application","files":["src/lib/training-plan-allocation.ts"],"detail":"In `applyHoursToActiveTrainingPlanCourse` (lines 233-241) and `advanceTrainingPlanAfterCheckride` / `manuallyActivateNextTrainingPlanCourse` (lines 357-365, 469-477), the active-course index is computed as `Number.isInteger(currentCourseIndex) ? clamp(...) : Math.max(0, courseAllocations.findIndex(a => a.status === 'active'))`. When no allocation has status 'active' (e.g. plan freshly created and never manually activated, or every course finished and none advanced), `findIndex` returns -1, and `Math.max(0, -1)` silently resolves to index 0 — the first course in the array — regardless of its real status (could be completed, upcoming, or hours_complete).","impact":"Flight/ground/simulator hours logged for a student can be silently credited to the wrong certificate allocation (e.g. a completed Private Pilot course instead of the actual in-progress Instrument rating). This corrupts flightHoursUsed/groundHoursUsed/simulatorHoursUsed on the wrong course, which feeds training-hour guardrails, payment schedules, and quote/invoice totals — a hard-to-detect data integrity bug with financial and FAA hour-tracking consequences. Confirmed live call sites: src/server/routes/routes-locations.ts (~lines 11446, 19985, 20081, 20290) and src/server/routes/routes-checkrides.ts:317.","recommendation":"When findIndex returns -1 (no active course and no valid stored index), return an explicit failure (applied: false, or a distinct reason like 'no_active_course') instead of defaulting to index 0. Callers should surface this as an operator-visible error rather than silently applying hours to an arbitrary course.","confidence":"high"}
confirmed=true only if the defect genuinely exists. If misread → verdict="false-positive". If real but wrong severity → set correctedSeverity. If real but underspecified → verdict="needs-detail" (kept). Return JSON per the schema.

